# Bifrost — upcoming milestones

## Audio device support

Goal: bring audio devices into Bifrost as first-class citizens alongside lights,
with the same provider/registry pattern and a clean REST API. The API surface is
what the companion MCP project (separate repo) will call to let an AI assistant
control the whole home.

### AudioProvider trait  [ ]
Define a trait analogous to LightProvider covering:
  - discover() → Vec<AudioDevice>
  - get_state(device_id) → AudioState { power, volume (0–100), mute, source, now_playing? }
  - set_state(device_id, AudioCommand { power?, volume?, mute?, source? })
Add AudioProviderFactory + AudioProviderRegistry (or extend ProviderRegistry).
Persist credentials encrypted (AES-256-GCM), same as lights.

### Sonos provider  [ ]
Protocol: Sonos S2 local HTTP API (REST/JSON, no cloud required).
  - Discovery: SSDP multicast on 239.255.255.250:1900, filter ST: urn:schemas-upnp-org:device:ZonePlayer:1
  - Control: POST http://<ip>:1400/json/* endpoints (playerVolume, playerTransportState, groupVolume, etc.)
  - State poll: GET /json/playerVolume, /json/playerTransportState
  - Group awareness: Sonos households → groups → players; expose groups as "zones"
Provider type string: "sonos"
Credential fields: none required (pure LAN), optional bind_addr
Tests: wiremock against the JSON endpoints; mock SSDP via loopback UDP (same pattern as govee-lan)

### Onkyo / Integra provider  [ ]
Protocol: eISCP (Ethernet Integra Serial Control Protocol) over TCP port 60128.
  - Discovery: UDP broadcast on port 60128, ISCP "!xECNQSTN" discovery packet
  - Commands: ISCP message framing — 4-byte "ISCP" magic, header len, data len, version, data ("!1PWR01", "!1MVL32", etc.)
  - Key commands: PWR (power), MVL (master volume 0–64 hex or 0–200 in 0.5dB steps), AMT (mute), SLI (input selector)
  - State: send QSTR queries, parse responses
Provider type string: "onkyo"
Credential fields: host (required), port (default 60128)
Tests: loopback TCP mock device that speaks eISCP framing, records commands

### Audio API routes  [ ]
Mirror the lights API shape so the MCP can treat audio and lights uniformly:
  GET    /api/audio/devices              → list all discovered audio devices
  GET    /api/audio/devices/:id          → single device state
  PUT    /api/audio/devices/:id/state    → set power / volume / mute / source
  GET    /api/audio/zones                → Sonos groups or Onkyo zones
  PUT    /api/audio/zones/:id/state      → group-level control
Auth: session cookie (same as all other routes). All routes return 401 if unauthenticated.

### Audio on the Dashboard / Floor Plan  [ ]
- Dashboard: audio zone cards alongside room (light) cards
- Floor Plan: room controller optionally linked to an audio zone (volume + mute toggle)
- Settings: add/remove audio providers, discover devices

---

## Companion MCP server  (separate repo — bifrost-mcp)  [ ]

A Model Context Protocol server that wraps the Bifrost REST API as MCP tools,
so an AI assistant (Claude, Whisper + LLM pipeline, etc.) can control the home
through natural language.

Planned tools:
  - list_rooms / list_lights / list_audio_devices
  - set_room_scene(room_id, scene_name_or_id)
  - set_light(light_id, { on, brightness, color })
  - set_audio(device_or_zone_id, { power, volume, mute, source })
  - get_home_state() → snapshot of all rooms + audio zones
  - apply_scene(scene_name) → apply to all rooms at once (whole-home scene)

Auth: Bifrost API key (generated in Settings, stored in MCP config, never in Bifrost DB plaintext).
Transport: stdio MCP (works with Claude Desktop, claude CLI --mcp, etc.)
Language: likely TypeScript (MCP SDK ecosystem), separate git repo.
